# Architecture

Source CSV
-> Bronze
-> Silver
-> Gold
-> Dashboard

## Bronze Responsibilities (Implemented)

- Raw CSV ingestion with PySpark.
- Explicit schema handling.
- Structural input validation.
- Parquet output storage.
- Ingestion metadata capture.
- Strict raw-data preservation.

Bronze must not perform business cleansing, deduplication, filtering of invalid FKs, or analytical transformations.

## Silver Responsibilities (Planned)

- Consume Bronze Parquet datasets.
- Perform data-quality checks:
  - completeness checks
  - uniqueness checks
  - referential integrity checks
  - business-rule checks
- Apply required transformations/standardization.
- Handle quality status/result tracking.
- Manage valid/invalid records per assignment requirements.

## Gold Responsibilities (Planned)

- Build business-facing aggregates and KPI datasets.
- Prepare analytics-ready outputs for dashboard consumption.

## Design Boundary

- Keep stage logic separated.
- Avoid back-porting Silver/Gold logic into Bronze.
- Preserve reproducibility and configuration-driven behavior across stages.
